id: pm-vcs-9c77
title: "Content-addressed object store: blobs, trees, commits and records"
description: "Four object kinds framed as '<type> <byteLength>\\0<payload>' and addressed by SHA-256 over the whole frame, so identical content always yields an identical id. Blobs hold bytes, trees hold sorted (mode, name, id) entries, commits hold a tree plus zero or more parents with author and message, and records hold a structured document as canonically ordered fields - the kind that makes per-field merging possible. Loose objects are zlib-deflated and written through a temp file plus rename so a torn write can never leave a half object under a valid id."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[1]: "area:vcs"
created_at: "2026-07-30T22:37:52.785Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-30T22:55:27.863Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
acceptance_criteria: Round-tripping any object of any kind returns byte-identical content; the same content written twice produces one object and one id; a corrupted payload is detected on read rather than returned; concurrent writers of the same object cannot observe a partial file
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
